# Docker builds run from the repository root because the Python workspace is
# only resolvable there. Keep the context to what a build actually needs.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Environments and caches — rebuilt inside the image, and a host `.venv`
# contains absolute paths that are wrong in a container.
#
# The `**/` matters: a bare `node_modules` matches only the context root, so
# without it `apps/web/node_modules` — the one that actually exists, and which
# holds platform-specific binaries compiled for the host — would be shipped
# into the build context.
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.uv-cache

# Local-only and never shipped.
spec/
.claude
.env
.env.*
*.log

# Build outputs.
**/.next
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
